        {
          "id": 594745181,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "It looks like all of our QCustomPlot-based widgets still render in light mode only, including the I/O Graphs. We can get away with `color().darker()` right now, but it probably wouldn't hurt to future-proof this with something like\n\n`bars_->setPen(QPen(ColorUtils::alphaBlend(color_, palette().windowText(), 0.65));`\n\npalette().windowText() *should* be either black or white depending our dark or light mode, and this will make the border color darker or lighter as appropriate. A blend ratio of 0.65 is just a guess based on what we do elsewhere in the code.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789948913",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
